.md\", \"line\": 67, \"claim_text\": \"The live line-drawing at the lower-court level tracks how the circuits draw the **active-inducement / passive-listening-post** boundary for jailhouse informants and the **point-of-attachment quantum** for pre-charge appearances\", \"class\": \"open-question\", \"subject\": \"Lower-court active-inducement/attachment-quantum frontier\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"jailhouse informant active inducement listening post\", \"point of attachment quantum pre-charge frontier\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0168\", \"file\": \"content/use-of-force-and-liability/Qualified Immunity.md\", \"line\": 67, \"claim_text\": \"A live **circuit divide** on the wrong-house-raid question\", \"class\": \"split\", \"subject\": \"Circuit divide on the wrong-house-raid qualified-immunity question (Jimerson)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"wrong house raid qualified immunity split\", \"Jimerson Garrison clearly established circuit divide\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0169\", \"file\": \"content/use-of-force-and-liability/Use of Force.md\", \"line\": 39, \"claim_text\": \"expressly **left open the \\\"officer-created danger\\\" question**\", \"class\": \"not-decided\", \"subject\": \"Barnes left open the officer-created-danger question\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"officer-created danger question left open\", \"Barnes v. Felix officer created danger reserved\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0170\", \"file\": \"content/use-of-force-and-liability/Use of Force.md\", \"line\": 41, \"claim_text\": \"did not resolve whether an officer's reckless pre-seizure conduct can bear on the reasonableness of the force itself\", \"class\": \"not-decided\", \"subject\": \"Whether reckless pre-seizure conduct bears on force reasonableness (Mendez/Barnes)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"reckless pre-seizure conduct force reasonableness\", \"Mendez Barnes officer created danger left open\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0171\", \"file\": \"content/use-of-force-and-liability/Use of Force.md\", \"line\": 75, \"claim_text\": \"Until the Court answers the reserved *[[Barnes v. Felix|Barnes]]* question, the practical rule is jurisdiction-specific\", \"class\": \"open-question\", \"subject\": \"Officer-created-danger rule is jurisdiction-specific until the Court answers Barnes\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"officer created danger jurisdiction-specific circuits\", \"Barnes reserved broad narrow reading circuits\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0172\", \"file\": \"content/warrant-exceptions/Consent Searches.md\", \"line\": 77, \"claim_text\": \"no SCOTUS consent-search case is currently pending\", \"class\": \"no-court-has\", \"subject\": \"No SCOTUS consent-search case currently pending; circuit law only\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"consent search no SCOTUS pending\", \"Jimeno scope circuit developments nationwide\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0173\", \"file\": \"content/warrant-exceptions/home-entry-and-search/Community Caretaking.md\", \"line\": 83, \"claim_text\": \"Role-based circuit/state developments only (**no SCOTUS\", \"class\": \"no-court-has\", \"subject\": \"No SCOTUS on the persons-in-public community-caretaking strand\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"community caretaking persons in public no SCOTUS\", \"Caniglia caretaking circuit law frontier\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0174\", \"file\": \"content/warrant-exceptions/home-entry-and-search/Destruction of Evidence.md\", \"line\": 60, \"claim_text\": \"Role-based, circuit/state only (**no SCOTUS\", \"class\": \"no-court-has\", \"subject\": \"No recent SCOTUS on the destruction-of-evidence exigency frontier\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"destruction of evidence exigency no SCOTUS\", \"Kentucky v. King manufactured exigency circuit\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0175\", \"file\": \"content/warrant-exceptions/home-entry-and-search/Entry to Arrest.md\", \"line\": 28, \"claim_text\": \"Whether staying outside the doorway defeats that protection is **unsettled — the Supreme Court has never decided it and the circuits divide\", \"class\": \"no-court-has\", \"subject\": \"SCOTUS has never decided constructive entry; circuits divide (rule box)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"constructive entry surround call out never decided\", \"Payton doorway coercion circuits divide\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0176\", \"file\": \"content/warrant-exceptions/home-entry-and-search/Entry to Arrest.md\", \"line\": 56, \"claim_text\": \"The Supreme Court has never decided whether coercing a suspect out of a surrounded home is a *[[Payton v. New York|Payton]]* in-home arrest, and the circuits divide\", \"class\": \"no-court-has\", \"subject\": \"SCOTUS has never decided whether coercing a suspect out is a Payton arrest; circuits divide\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"constructive entry Payton in-home arrest never decided\", \"surround and call out circuits divide\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0177\", \"file\": \"content/warrant-exceptions/home-entry-and-search/Entry to Arrest.md\", \"line\": 60, \"claim_text\": \"The **First, Third, Fourth, and Eighth Circuits** have no representative constructive-entry decision mapped in this build; do not assume how they come out\", \"class\": \"other\", \"subject\": \"First, Third, Fourth, Eighth Circuits unmapped on constructive entry\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"constructive entry unmapped circuits\", \"First Third Fourth Eighth Circuit no representative decision\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0178\", \"file\": \"content/warrant-exceptions/home-entry-and-search/Exigent Circumstances and Hot Pursuit.md\", \"line\": 82, \"claim_text\": \"Role-based, circuit/state only (**no SCOTUS\", \"class\": \"no-court-has\", \"subject\": \"No recent SCOTUS on the exigency frontier; no nationwide circuit rule\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"exigent circumstances no SCOTUS nationwide\", \"Hayden Santana continuity circuit developments\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0179\", \"file\": \"content/warrant-exceptions/home-entry-and-search/Securing the Scene.md\", \"line\": 69, \"claim_text\": \"Role-based circuit developments only (**no SCOTUS\", \"class\": \"no-court-has\", \"subject\": \"No recent SCOTUS on the scene-securing frontier\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"securing the scene no SCOTUS circuit\", \"scene-securing authorities margins circuit developments\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0180\", \"file\": \"content/warrant-exceptions/programmatic-and-special-needs-searches/Border Searches.md\", \"line\": 31, \"claim_text\": \"the Court reserved only that some property searches might be \\\"so destructive as to require a different result\", \"class\": \"not-decided\", \"subject\": \"Flores-Montano reserved whether some property searches are too destructive\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"border property search too destructive reserved\", \"Flores-Montano reserved destructive property search\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0181\", \"file\": \"content/warrant-exceptions/searching-a-vehicle/Automobile Exception.md\", \"line\": 71, \"claim_text\": \"the frontier is confined to whether a device's *data* is a \\\"container\\\" the exception can reach or a distinct privacy interest that demands its own warrant\", \"class\": \"open-question\", \"subject\": \"Whether a device's data is a 'container' within the automobile exception\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"automobile exception device data container\", \"vehicle search phone data separate warrant frontier\"]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
